==Battleground==
*1 [[Madhead (Enemy)|Madhead]] (300%) spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Madhead (Enemy)|Madhead]] (300%) spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Madhead (Enemy)|Madhead]] (300%) spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Madhead (Enemy)|Madhead]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**11 [[Madhead (Enemy)|Madheads]] (300%) spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
**7 [[Madhead (Enemy)|Madheads]] (300%) spawn after 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>, delay 10~15 seconds<sup>300f~450f</sup>.
**4 [[Madhead (Enemy)|Madheads]] (300%) spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 15~20 seconds<sup>450f~600f</sup>.
**2 [[Madhead (Enemy)|Madheads]] (300%) spawn after 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>, delay 20~25 seconds<sup>600f~750f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Madhead (Enemy)|Madhead]] can easily weaken any Cat unit that gets in melee range, and can use stepping stools to attack farther units, so it is best to bring primarily long ranged cats such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]], or any effective [[LD]] or Anti-[[Traitless]] Ubers. Since it is only Madhead, this strategy is effective, but with other pushers stronger units are required.

